BUG-42: do not mirror brackets after reversing a right-to-left PDF run when the font stores logical code points.

The PDF import writes a right-to-left run in visual (left to right) order and reverses it, mirroring every
Bidi_Mirrored code point on the way (SubstituteBidiMirrored). That is right for producers that store the
code point that LOOKS like the glyph ("(" reads "(" from left to right) and wrong for producers whose
ToUnicode stores the LOGICAL code point and draws the glyph mirrored (a closing ")" comes first in the
stream): the heading «بياناتي» came out as »بياناتي« in every build.

PDFIProcessor::noteBracketGlyph counts, per font FAMILY (subset prefix and style suffix dropped: a FontId is per
size and weight, which split the evidence of a heading font too thin) and in stream order, bracket pairs in lines
that have right-to-left letters: an opener followed by its closer is visual order, a closer with no opener before
it is a logical code point. isLogicalBracketFont(font id) is true only when the closer-first pairs are at least 3
and more than twice the opener-first ones. Both mirroring sites (Writer and Draw emitters) skip the mirroring for
such a font. No evidence, or a mix, keeps the old behaviour. Corpus measurement of the stream order (closer-first
vs opener-first): cma_board_guide 4 vs 70 (unchanged), fahr_ab0ae96a 160 vs 6, dghr_parttime_contract 22 vs 4,
fahr_5f757ead 9 vs 2 (changed), taqeem_draft_contract 57 vs 52 (mixed, unchanged).

KNOWN LIMITS (a review on 2026-11-02 listed them; an "edge adjacency" rework was measured and was WORSE, it flipped
visual-order documents, so they stay):
- a pair votes only when a right-to-left letter came earlier in the same chunk, and chunks split on any wide gap, so
  a bracket group at the very start of a chunk casts no vote (the family is usually decided by its other chunks);
- a Latin pair in a right-to-left chunk, "(DGHR)", votes "visual" and dilutes a logical family's count;
- a document whose bracket glyphs come from many subsets or producers pooled under one family name decides together.

ROUTING. This file is named *-pdf-docx.patch, which pipeline/lib/fingerprint.sh sends to the pdf-docx module ONLY.
The Draw emitter hunk is therefore not used (pdf-docx imports into Writer): PDF to PPTX keeps the old bracket
behaviour until the patch is routed to pdf-pptx as well, a separate decision whose output must be measured first.
The hunks avoid the lines that differ between the pdf-docx and pdf-pptx series (pdf-pptx lacks the BUG-28 guards in
pdfiprocessor.cxx, BUG-39); both series were replayed and the patch applies to each.

